{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall assign it to the service of the Tent of Meeting.</b> I have already mentioned that because in the sin of the calf they cut down the plantings and sinned by making the end into the beginning, therefore He commanded that the shekels — for they are a ransom for the soul — be for the service of the Tent of Meeting, namely the sockets (אדנים), which are the foundation and base of the Mishkan. For the Mishkan, which corresponds to the creation of the world, rested upon them. And because of this He said, ״והיה לבני ישראל לזכרון לפני ה׳ לכפר על נפשותיכם״ — and it shall be for the children of Israel a memorial before HaShem to make atonement for your souls — which declares that they would make in the structure a particular and designated thing from the silver of the shekels, and that thing would be for the children of Israel a memorial, for they would be reminded of their sin continually and take comfort in it, in the sense of (Psalms 51:5): ״וחטאתי נגדי תמיד״ — and my sin is ever before me; and it would be לפני ה׳ לכפר — before HaShem for atonement — for He would be reconciled to them through the sockets being the foundations of the Mishkan, and then they would turn the head upward. And therefore He called this silver כסף הכפורים — the silver of atonements." "<b>And the reason</b> the section of the Kiyyor (laver) was juxtaposed to the section of the Shekalim is that the waters of the laver increase the rains, and the shekels were charity, and by virtue of charity the rains increase, and when it is withheld they are held back. And so the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: the rains are held back only on account of those who pledge charity in public and do not give, as it is said (Proverbs 25:14): ״נשיאים ורוח וגשם אין איש מתהלל במתת שקר״ — clouds and wind and rain, but no man boasts of a false gift."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:41.837216275Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}